-- title:
--   Chart ring modulo varpi at a unique Gauss valuation
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a principal ideal domain with fraction field $K_0$, let $F$ be a field that is an extension of $K_0$ compatibly with its $R$-algebra structure, and let $j \in F$ be nonzero and transcendental over $R$, with $F$ finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$ obtained by adjoining $j$ to $K_0$ inside $F$. Let $\varpi \in R$ be prime and let $V \subseteq F$ be a valuation subring such that: the image of every element of $R$ lies in $V$; the image of $\varpi$ is a non-unit of $V$; for every $P \in R[X]$ with $\varpi$ (as a constant polynomial) not dividing $P$, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$; every non-unit $f$ of $V$ satisfies $f \cdot \varpi^{-1} \in V$; and $V$ is the unique valuation subring of $F$ satisfying the first three of these conditions. Write $\mathcal{O}$ for `chartAlgFin R F j`, the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $R[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {j}`. Then $\mathcal{O} \subseteq V$, the ideal $\varpi\mathcal{O}$ generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $\mathcal{O}$ is prime, and for $a \in \mathcal{O}$ one has $a \in \varpi\mathcal{O}$ if and only if $a$ is a non-unit of $V$.
--
--   This is the Deuring–Igusa reduction statement for the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model: under uniqueness and unramifiedness of the Gauss-type extension of the $\varpi$-adic valuation, $\varpi\mathcal{O} = \mathfrak{m}_V \cap \mathcal{O}$, so the special fibre of the chart is integral with generic point the Gauss valuation. It is used in the analysis of minimal primes over $\varpi$ in chart rings of modular curves and in the integrality of the relevant tensor products.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_span_singleton_isPrime_and_mem_iff_mem_nonunits_of_valuationSubring.lean

